35,2,1,talk,Servas,,"Interestingly, narrow tools for one trade survived, while those requiring daily entry from everyone failed. Standardization efforts often ended without an owner.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The capital line is frozen, but we have room in the software allowance. Also, per-head licences are getting more expensive, while fixed-fees are stable.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Sakura,,Oh no! Network coverage at plants is terrible—half the time it's gone! And our developers are busy with accounting until Q3!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"We are losing an hour daily to copying records, and misrouted deliveries are happening because different units have different addresses for the same firm.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The coordination group is understaffed and writing logs by hand. Plus, as Sakura noted, our developers are unavailable and the old interfaces are undocumented.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Ryuji, the record-copying and address errors suggest a need for a central truth, but @Asuka's point about staffing makes a large system risky.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"If we use the software allowance, we should avoid per-head licences. A fixed-fee project would be much safer for our current budget.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"If we can't use the network at plants, any app for technicians is going to be a disaster unless it works offline!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,The waste is clear. We are duplicating data and shipping things to the wrong places. This is a systemic failure of data management.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,We have no developers and a depleted coordination group. Whatever we pick must not require heavy internal lifting or constant manual updates.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,"We must avoid a ""everyone must use it"" tool. A narrow, specific solution that solves a concrete problem is more likely to survive.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Asuka, if the developers are gone, can we even afford an outside vendor with the frozen capital budget?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Sakura,,Maybe something that doesn't need a huge build? Or something that doesn't rely on the plant Wi-Fi?,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,The data duplication is the most logical target. It's a daily loss of time and a cause of delivery errors.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"But a ""Data Hub"" sounds like it would require the very coordination and developer time we currently lack.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Servas,,We must weigh the pain of the current waste against the risk of project collapse.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I agree. We need the most conservative path.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Sakura,,I just don't want to promise something that won't work in the field!,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,The evidence of waste is too significant to ignore.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I will support a project only if it doesn't break the remaining staff.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
