60,3,1,talk,Servas,,"We have four candidates: A: Supplier Data Hub, B: Workflow Assistant, C: Training Studio, and D: Field Service App.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Candidate A sounds expensive if it's per-user. Candidate B and C seem smaller, but A solves the address issues Ryuji found.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"Candidate D is out! I saw the network reports; it'll fail. Candidate B sounds fun, but is it actually useful?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Candidate A directly addresses the misrouted deliveries and the time lost to copying records. It is the most logical choice.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Candidate A requires cross-unit standardization, which Servas said usually fails. Candidate B or C are less burdensome on staff.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Ryuji, while A solves the problem, history shows that broad standardization fails. A narrow tool is better. Candidate C is quite narrow.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"Candidate C, the Training Studio, might be a fixed-fee production. That would fit our software allowance and avoid the frozen capital line.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Sakura,,But does the Training Studio stop the misrouted deliveries? I think Candidate A is better if we can just make it simple.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, the ""burden"" of A is less than the current burden of losing an hour a day to manual copying.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"Not if the project fails and we've wasted the fund. Candidate B is a shared tool, but it might just be more ""daily entry"" that people ignore.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Servas,,"I lean toward Candidate C. It's a production unit, not a system everyone must maintain daily. It's sustainable.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I'm worried about A's long-term costs. I think C is the safest financial bet.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Sakura,,"I'll go with A! It's the most exciting and solves the biggest mess, even if it's hard.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I cannot ignore the incident logs. Candidate A is the only one that stops the actual errors on the floor.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"I cannot support A. The lack of developers and coordination staff makes a ""Hub"" a fantasy. I vote for C.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Servas,,It seems we are split between the practical need for data and the practical reality of our resources.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I'll stick with C.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Sakura,,I'm staying with A!,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I'm staying with A.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I'm staying with C.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
